ference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:110:| Source/derived provenance authored from output | `test/inference-adapter.test.ts` metadata assertions | Provenance equals assignment provider/model/prompt and deterministic provider has none | Model text could accidentally contain plausible provenance strings |\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:156:3. Call the host `ModelCall` with the kind's provider/model assignment.\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:137:| Inference Host | **Yes** | The `ModelCall` implementation, assignment config, startup validation |\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:151:      thread-resolution.ts         NEW  launch flags → registry (new / --session / --continue / --resume); partial-id match\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:162:      assignments.ts               NEW  config load + shape validation (the seven kinds)\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:163:      startup-validation.ts        NEW  registry existence + auth-availability probe; reporting (ctx.ui/headless)\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:184:| `lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts` | NEW | Launch flags → registry resolution (new / `--session` full+partial / `--continue` most-recent); reload reconstructs from resolved id; unresolvable id fails loud | `lhc` threads | AC-1.2, AC-1.5, AC-1.6 |\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:194:| `inference/assignments.ts` | NEW | Load seven assignments from config; fail loud on missing/unknown/placeholder; override on next start | — | AC-5.4, AC-5.5 |\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:195:| `inference/startup-validation.ts` | NEW | Probe each assignment with `modelRegistry.find(provider, model)` for existence and `hasConfiguredAuth(model)` / `getAvailable()` membership for configured auth; report unknown and not-logged-in lanes through `ctx.ui`/headless diagnostics; leave capture running | PI modelRegistry | AC-5.1, AC-5.2, AC-5.3 |\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:266:| Resolve thread from launch | `lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts` | `resolveThread(launch: LaunchFlags, pi: ExtensionAPI): Promise<OpResult<ThreadRef>>` | registry resolve/create by mode; partial-id match; loud on unresolvable; structured `OpResult` |\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:393:Before any derivation runs, the connector checks that all seven assignments point at lanes PI can actually reach, so a misconfiguration surfaces up front rather than as a derivation failure later. Two layers do two different jobs, and conflating them would be wrong. The SDK already validates assignment *shape* at construction — all seven kinds present, non-empty provider/model, prompt-name registered — and throws if not; that is `assignments.ts`'s \"fail loud\" (AC-5.5), and it is enforced by LHC, not re-implemented here. The connector adds a *reachability* probe on top: for each assignment, first call `ctx.modelRegistry.find(provider, model)` to distinguish an unknown provider/model from a known lane, then check configured auth with `ctx.modelRegistry.hasConfiguredAuth(model)` or equivalent `getAvailable()` membership. Unknown lanes report a config/assignment fix; known-but-unauthed lanes report a login/auth fix. OAuth freshness is still verified at runtime by the model-call path and classified as a derivation failure if the token is stale.\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:401:| Load + shape-validate | `inference/assignments.ts` | `loadAssignments(config): Record<FormKind, ModelAssignment>` | throws on missing/unknown/placeholder |\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:402:| Reachability probe | `inference/startup-validation.ts` | `validateReachable(assignments, ctx): ValidationReport` | structured report |\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:403:| Report | `inference/startup-validation.ts` | `report(r, ctx, state): void` | `ctx.ui` when available; structured state diagnostic always |\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:442:// lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts — AC-1.2, 1.5, 1.6\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:496:// inference/assignments.ts — AC-5.4, 5.5\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:501:// inference/startup-validation.ts — AC-5.1, 5.2, 5.3\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:503:  unreachable: {\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:512:  assignments: Record<FormKind, ModelAssignment>,\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:541:| Persistence / Restart | `lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts` | Discard the in-memory holder, re-resolve the same thread by its id from the registry, capture continues on it | The AC says \"resume on the resolved thread\"; only a real reopen proves resolution works across process death without a retained object |\n./docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:672:**Scope:** shape validation (LHC-enforced), reachability probe using existence + configured-auth checks, `ctx.ui`/headless reporting, config override. **ACs:** 5.1–5.5. **Relevant sections:** Flow 5, `inference/{assignments,startup-validation}.ts`. **Risk shape:** validation independent of capture; reporting must not assume a TUI.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:11:| AC-1.3 | Story 2 | complete assignment validation |\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:40:| TC-5.3 | Story 6 | Epic 03 regression legs |\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:54:| Host supplies inference config | Story 2 | TC-1.1 | exactly one of `provider` / `inference`; complete assignments required |\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/coverage.md:64:| Epic 03 boundary contracts survive trigger move | Story 6 | TC-5.3 | forward-only, short form, compact reset, deterministic replay, and failure visibility hold |\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/04-derivation-state-report-repair.md:144:| 2026-06-11 | TC-4.2's suggested mechanism (`maxItems: 1` + backoff 0 to stop between attempts) is unreachable: non-terminal failed attempts never count toward `maxItems`, and with backoff 0 the head is immediately re-claimable. Implemented with an injected frozen clock + non-zero backoff: the drain stops `waiting` with the item durably mid-retry — same observable contract (`pending` + queue `{attempts: 1, lastError}`), fully deterministic | Implementation detail of the test; AC-4.2 asserted as specified |\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:141:- The corrupt fixture is the one sanctioned below-SDK write — direct insert of a second open-turn row, possible only because the contract makes the state unreachable through any operation.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/04-turn-state-machine/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:283:| TC-5.3 | cross-thread keys | same key, two threads | both record |\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:47:- **TC-5.3** (AC-5.5): amended `view-boundary.test.ts` plus new turn-end file\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:98:- [test-plan.md §TC-5.1 / TC-5.2 / TC-5.3](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/test-plan.md:106), lines 106-125\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:109:| TC-5.3 | amended `test/view-boundary.test.ts` plus new turn-end file | monotonicity, short form, compact reset, deterministic replay, failure injection, next-close heal |\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:206:- TC-5.1, TC-5.2, and TC-5.3 are green.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:4:You are the story lead for `02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment` on durable story run `02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment-story-run-001`.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:19:Path: /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/stories/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment.md\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:27:Add the `createSdk` inference construction path: one host model-call function plus complete per-kind model assignments.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:34:**Objective:** Establish the production inference seam and validate model assignments loudly at SDK construction.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:36:**Scope In:** `provider` XOR `inference`, `ModelCall` contract, complete assignment validation, adapter construction wiring, and per-call provider/model routing.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:45:- **AC-1.1**: `createSdk` accepts exactly one of `provider` (a `DerivationProvider`, unchanged) or `inference` (model-call function + assignments). Both supplied, or neither, is a caller error naming the rule.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:48:- **AC-1.4**: Per-call routing: each drained work item looks up its kind's assignment and the function receives that assignment's provider and model strings. Different kinds routing to different providers in one config work item-by-item with no cross-kind interference.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:55:  - unknown kind key in assignments returns `TypeError` naming it\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:58:  - empty `provider` or `model` string in one assignment returns `TypeError`\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:72:This story establishes the SDK construction boundary for real inference. `createSdk` accepts exactly one provider arrival path: direct `provider` injection or `inference` config. On the inference path, SDK validation resolves the assignment map and builds the real adapter into the same `DerivationProvider` slot the deterministic provider already uses.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:74:The external boundary is the host-supplied `ModelCall`. LHC owns provider/model assignment and prompt selection; the host owns credentialed transport.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:154:  assignments: Record<FormKind, ModelAssignment>;\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:170:  assignments: {\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:190:| empty provider/model | assignment field and kind |\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:195:- Do not accept partial assignment maps.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:201:- Entrypoint: `createSdk({ inference: { call, assignments } })`.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:219:- Inference assignments validate all seven `FormKind`s, reject unknown keys, reject unknown prompts, and reject empty provider/model strings.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:246:| `test/view-boundary.test.ts` (amended) + `test/view-boundary-turn-end.test.ts` (new) | default | TC-5.1, TC-5.2, TC-5.3 |\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:255:- `recordingCall(responses: Record<FormKind, string>)` → `{ call: ModelCall, log: ModelCallInput[] }`. Resolves each call with the kind's canned text (kind inferred from the assignment the test built — in practice keyed by `model` string, which tests assign uniquely per kind). Every input pushed to `log`.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:259:- `validAssignments(overrides?)` → a complete seven-kind assignment map for construction tests, each kind assigned a distinct fake provider/model string.\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:265:**`test/fixtures/seam-conformance.ts`** (Chunk 0) — the parameterized contract assertions (DD-13): `assertModelCallContract(call)` (shape of success/failure results on a probe call) and `assertRoutingThroughSdk(call, assignments)` (TC-1.2's routing assertions extracted so TC-4.3 runs them against the real host unchanged).\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:275:- unknown kind key in assignments → `TypeError` naming it\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:278:- empty `provider`/`model` string in one assignment → `TypeError`\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:293:- each form's `metadata.provenance` equals its assignment `{ provider, model, prompt }`; deterministic-provider forms carry none\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:348:### TC-5.3 — Epic 03 contract regression under the new trigger (AC-5.5)\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:404:| Boundary decision and status sum diverge | shared-query invariant + TC-5.3's status leg after each advance |\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:435:Path: /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/001-current.json\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/artifacts/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:439:storyRunId: \"02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment-story-run-001\"\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference